QuickStart Guide :: cam_aqua_fv
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
description:        basic configuration
cloud physics:      "RK" or "MG"
surface type:       slab ocean aquaplanet
dynamical core:     finite volume
radiation scheme:   ExoRT 2.0, ExoRT/3dmodels/src.cam.exort

== create the case ==
create_newcase -case $my_aquaplanet_case_name -res f45_f45 -mach discover -compset E2000C4AQI


== set levels, physics, and the ExoRT radiative transfer package ==
-- default command below uses "RK" (i.e. cam4) clouds.
xmlchange CAM_CONFIG_OPTS="-nlev 40 -phys cam4 -usr_src $EXORT_PATH/ExoRT/3dmodels/src.cam.exort"

-- command below builds with "MG" (cam5) clouds 
xmlchange CAM_CONFIG_OPTS="-nlev 40 -phys cam4 -usr_src $EXORT_PATH/ExoRT/3dmodels/src.cam.exort -chem none -microphys mg1"


== transfer files ==
install SourceMods into your $Case directory (shared tree + this config's files):
     $EXOCAM/cesm1.2.1/install_sourcemods.sh cam_aqua_fv $CASEROOT/SourceMods
copy namelist files into your $Case directory
     for "MG" clouds, uncomment blocks in user_nl_cam


== point ExoRT at its data ==
set exort_rootdir in $EXORT_PATH/ExoRT/3dmodels/src.cam.exort/sys_rootdir.F90
set exo_solar_file in $CASEROOT/SourceMods/src.share/exoplanet_mod.F90
     to an 84-band file, $EXORT_PATH/ExoRT/data/stellar/*_n84.nc
keep NTHRDS_ATM = 1

== finish ==
build and run



---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
NOTES:
$EXORT_PATH is the path	where ExoRT is located

for instance... 
on Summit; $EXORT_PATH = /projects/wolfet/models
on Hyak;   $EXORT_PATH = /suppscr/vsm/gscratch/wolfet
on Discover; $EXOC_PATH = $EXORT_PATH = /discover/nobackup/etwolf/models
